6136-2023-ER-F0292 P1 1(a)(iii) p153 (iii) Fairly answered. However, some candidates failed to differentiate between types of development indicators and examples of each indicator, e.g social as a development indicator and health as an example of social indicator.
6136-2023-ER-F0293 P1 1(a)(iv) p153 (iv) Fairly answered. Most candidates could score two marks for improvement in health care and clean water. However, some candidates confused life expectancy and population growth or had no idea on what it means to “project”.
6136-2023-ER-F0294 P1 1(b) p153 (b) Well answered. Few candidates referred to all political indicators, without stating those that cannot be used for measuring development.
6136-2023-ER-F0295 P1 1(c)(i) p153 (c) (i) Well answered. Few candidates could not recall all the disadvantages of GDP as a development indicator.
6136-2023-ER-F0297 P1 1(d)(i) p154 (d) (i) Fairly well answered. Some candidates could only define conservation and failed to state that “it encourages economic growth”.
